{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse","lean:module:QOU.Glossary","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.descartes_terminal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.descartes_terminal","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse.lean#L138-L147","doc":"**Terminality of Bring's surface in C_{-6}.**\nFor every Descartes universe (C, A, ω, q), the Euler characteristic\nis −6 and fibre-preserving monoidal functors are rigid (unique up to\nnatural isomorphism).\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{thm:descartes}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.TannakaKreinRigidity.rigid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.TannakaKreinRigidity.rigid","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse.lean#L136-L136","doc":"Rigidity: the isomorphism count equals 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.TannakaKreinRigidity.iso_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.TannakaKreinRigidity.iso_count","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse.lean#L134-L134","doc":"The number of natural isomorphisms between any two fibre-preserving\nmonoidal functors with the same fibre functor.  Tannaka–Krein\nrigidity says this is exactly 1 (up to iso). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.TannakaKreinRigidity.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.TannakaKreinRigidity.mk","kind":"ctor","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse.lean#L130-L130","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.TannakaKreinRigidity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.TannakaKreinRigidity","kind":"structure","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse.lean#L127-L136","doc":"**Terminality data**: packages the Tannaka–Krein rigidity argument.\nA fibre-preserving monoidal functor between Tannakian categories over\nthe same fibre functor is unique up to natural isomorphism. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ChiralSectorCoords.b","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ChiralSectorCoords.b","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse.lean#L123-L123","doc":"Blue chiral coordinate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ChiralSectorCoords.g","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ChiralSectorCoords.g","kind":"def","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse.lean#L121-L121","doc":"Green chiral coordinate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ChiralSectorCoords.r","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ChiralSectorCoords.r","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse.lean#L119-L119","doc":"Red chiral coordinate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ChiralSectorCoords.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ChiralSectorCoords.mk","kind":"ctor","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse.lean#L117-L117","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ChiralSectorCoords","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ChiralSectorCoords","kind":"structure","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse.lean#L112-L123","doc":"**Chiral sector coordinates** `(r, g, b)`: the three chiral\ncoordinates on Bring's surface, corresponding to the three roots\nof the chiral cubic.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:chiral-sector-coords}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ExceptionalDivisor.fibre_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ExceptionalDivisor.fibre_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse.lean#L110-L110","doc":"The fibre is non-empty. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ExceptionalDivisor.fibre","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ExceptionalDivisor.fibre","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse.lean#L108-L108","doc":"The exceptional fibre type (abstractly CP¹). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ExceptionalDivisor.point","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ExceptionalDivisor.point","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse.lean#L106-L106","doc":"The singular point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ExceptionalDivisor.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ExceptionalDivisor.mk","kind":"ctor","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse.lean#L104-L104","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ExceptionalDivisor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ExceptionalDivisor","kind":"structure","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse.lean#L99-L110","doc":"**Exceptional divisor at a point** `p`: the fibre of the blow-up\nat a singular point of the descent map.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:exceptional-divisor}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.genus_of_maximal_descent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.genus_of_maximal_descent","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse.lean#L70-L82","doc":"**Proposition (Genus of the maximal descent)**: if a Descartes universe\ndescends to a compact one-complex-dimensional variety `M₀`, then `M₀`\nis a Riemann surface of genus `g = 4`.\n\nProof: `χ = 2 − 2g = −6` gives `g = 4`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:genus-maximal-descent}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.DescartesUniverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.DescartesUniverse","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse.lean#L47-L49","doc":"A shorthand: a **Descartes universe** is a QOU satisfying the Descartes\ncondition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ArchimedeanCondition.descartes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ArchimedeanCondition.descartes","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse.lean#L44-L44","doc":"The Descartes condition: `χ(E) = −6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ArchimedeanCondition.eulerChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ArchimedeanCondition.eulerChar","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse.lean#L42-L42","doc":"The Euler characteristic of the bulk bundle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ArchimedeanCondition.cqou","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ArchimedeanCondition.cqou","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse.lean#L40-L40","doc":"The ℂ quantum observable universe. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ArchimedeanCondition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ArchimedeanCondition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse.lean#L38-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ArchimedeanCondition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.ArchimedeanCondition","kind":"structure","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse.lean#L32-L44","doc":"**Descartes condition**: a ℂ quantum observable universe satisfies\nthe Descartes condition if the Euler characteristic of the bulk\nbundle is `χ(E) = −6`.  A QOU satisfying this is a *Descartes universe*.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:archimedean-condition}` ","signatureChunk":0}]}